| The `strings` module is the first first-party module written in Rust on
| `code-native` (rather than C on `runtime.c` directly) — see the module's
| README for why the split exists. `Shout` is the inherited handler: it used
| to live in `test_math`, and the split proposal hands it over here. Same
| contract byte-for-byte: uppercase the ASCII letters, append `!`.
link "native_modules/strings.so" as s
emit Shout { value = "whisper" } to s get n
assert n = { _class = "ShoutResult", value = "WHISPER!" }
